## Next Recommended Step

Do not move directly from this handoff into original asset mutation or solver
unit expansion. The next safe action is to keep the Phase 3 transaction
hardening contract in
`Docs/Analysis/controlrig_stable_authoring_phase3_contract.md` green and keep
the Phase 4 stable fixture contract in
`Docs/Analysis/controlrig_stable_authoring_phase4_contract.md` green, then run a
separate Ieta-reviewed Phase 4 sample-temp proof pass from the filesystem-only
release gate. Use only `/Game/_MCP_Temp` or `/Game/_MCP_Sample` targets when
Unreal Editor and the bridge are intentionally available.

Phase 5 solver work remains blocked until the sample/temp controls-only fixture
has passing build, compile, readback, dependency-audit, and cleanup evidence.
The current Phase 4 commandlet proof is recorded in
`Docs/Analysis/controlrig_stable_authoring_phase4_live_proof.md`; it does not approve solver work by itself. Keep
`Docs/Analysis/controlrig_stable_authoring_phase5_contract.md` green until a
separate reviewed task explicitly approves solver unit expansion.
